   "type": "done",
   "answer": "## AMAT Calculation\n\n**Formula** (from the lecture, p. 26 [S2] and p. 27 [S1]):\n\n$$\\text{AMAT} = \\text{Hit Time} + \\text{Miss Rate} \\times \\text{Miss Penalty}$$\n\n**Given values** (matching the worked example on p. 27 [S1]):\n- Hit Time = 1 cycle\n- Miss Rate = 10% = 0.1\n- Miss Penalty = 300 cycles\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n$$\\text{AMAT} = 1 + 0.1 \\times 300 = 1 + 30 = \\boxed{31 \\text{ cycles}}$$\n\n**Reasoning:** On average, every memory access takes the 1-cycle hit time, and additionally 10% of accesses incur the 300-cycle miss penalty. The expected penalty contribution is 0.1 × 300 = 30 cycles, giving a total average of 31 cycles.\n\n**Sources:**\n- [S1] p. 27 — \"AMAT = Hit Time + Miss rate * Miss Penalty\" with the exact example: \"Cache Hit = 1 cycle, Miss rate = 10% = 0.1, Miss penalty = 300 cycles → AMAT = 1 + 0.1 * 300 = 31 cycles\"\n- [S2] p. 26 — General AMAT formula and definition of miss penalty",
   "citations": [
